{"encoding":"verislop.formalizer-capability-gap/0.1","obligation_ids":["D1","A1","O1","O2","O3","O4","O5","O6","O7","O8","I1","S1","N1"],"gaps":[{"obligation_ids":["O8"],"feature":"Contract-metadata inspection and verification-stage predicates","reason":"O8 is a required guarantee without allowed assumptions. It requires preservation of obligation kinds, roles and required flags, independent source-facet checks against kernel-reconstructed contracts before proof, after acceptance and at closure, and the specified trusted verification boundary. The provided term, formula and source-requirement grammars cannot refer to obligation metadata, kernel-reconstructed contracts, verification stages or trust-boundary configuration. Consequently they cannot express O8's complete guarantee without substituting an unrelated value or source proposition.","attempted_representations":["The functional aggregation can use sorted unique mapped group strings, an exact integer ceiling-derived list_range for bucket indices, event filters preserving duplicate occurrences, exact integer sums, and total folds carrying an optional previous sum and ordered output records. These supported constructions preserve nullable values, causal filling and group-major order, but cannot inspect the proposal's obligation metadata or verification workflow.","Mixed universal value formulas and source_requirements can retain the solve endpoint and all seven closed source properties for O1 through O7; source-only rows can retain I1 and S1. Their constructors do not express the separate requirement that reconstructed contracts be checked at three verification stages or that specified components remain explicitly trusted.","Binding O8 to an existing source theorem, True, a reflexive equality or a conjunction of aggregation equations would omit its metadata, staged-checking and trust-boundary requirements. No supported additional caller assumption can supply those requirements because O8 permits none."]}]}